Subject: [PATCH 13/13] amd64: compile the Forth loader in (TODO 13.1)

CONFIG_LOADER_FORTH is true on x86 and was false on amd64. It gates
libopenbios/forth_load.c and the is_forth() arm of libopenbios/initprogram.c,
so without it the generic loader chain has no Forth entry at all.

THIS IS A PREREQUISITE AND IT IS INERT TODAY, which is stated here rather than
left for a reader to infer from a landed config change. TODO 13.1's checkpoint
-- "a .fth loaded off media prints its own marker" -- CANNOT be reached, and
x86 fails identically, so the blocker is not the port's:

  0 > load /ide@1/cdrom@0:\marker.fth
  Mounted iso9660
  Path=/marker.fth
  Unable to locate (init-program)!

`boot <file>` never consults this chain on either arch -- arch/{x86,amd64}/boot.c
call linux_load() and nothing else -- so the chain is reached through `load` ->
`$load`, which ends with `init-program`, which is
`s" (init-program)" $find if execute else ." Unable to locate..." then`.

Probed at the prompt: `dup`, `is-cfunc`, `(does>)` and `platform-boot` are all
FOUND; `(init-program)` and `(go)` are MISSING -- on amd64 AND on x86. So $find
works, bind_func works, and precisely the two words bound inside openbios_init()
are unreachable. `platform-boot`, bound by bind_func later in the same
arch_init() after device_end(), is found.

Two hypotheses were tested and both are refuted:

  - "parenthesised names are not findable" -- (does>) is found.
  - "is-cfunc uses $create, which defines into the current vocabulary, so an
    active device context swallows them" -- adding device_end() before
    openbios_init() gave `set_property: NULL phandle` and a general protection
    fault at 08:0000000000102ba3, named by Spike 2's handler. Reverted.

Cause is recorded as UNKNOWN rather than guessed at. The next probe that would
separate "openbios_init() is never called here" from "it is called and its words
land somewhere unreachable" is a throwaway marker bound as its first statement.

What this patch does assert: the build is clean, and neither `smoke-openbios.sh
amd64` nor `amd64-linux` regressed.

CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA -- 13.1's other flip -- is deliberately NOT changed. Its
checkpoint is `byte-load` reached at all, and drivers/pci.c:1045's feval lives in
vga_config_cb, which runs only while enumerating a VGA-class PCI device. amd64
never enumerates PCI: arch/x86 calls ob_pci_init() and then ob_ide_init on the
probed path, arch/amd64 calls only ob_ide_init against a hardcoded
"/pci/pci-ata". Flipping it would compile a driver nothing can call. (And that
feval is not itself guarded by CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA, so an arch that DID enumerate
PCI with VGA off would execute an undefined word -- masked here only by the
missing enumeration.) Wiring ob_pci_init() into amd64 is Spike-sized and belongs
in its own item.

--- a/config/examples/amd64_config.xml
+++ b/config/examples/amd64_config.xml
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
   <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_BOOTINFO" type="boolean" value="false"/>
   <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_ELF" type="boolean" value="true"/>
   <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_FCODE" type="boolean" value="false"/>
-  <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_FORTH" type="boolean" value="false"/>
+  <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_FORTH" type="boolean" value="true"/>
   <option name="CONFIG_LOADER_XCOFF" type="boolean" value="false"/>
 
   <!-- Filesystem Configuration -->
